+# Optional live level-editor MCP bridge
+
+This is a modified Sauerbraten source tree with an opt-in local editor bridge.
+An external Python server exposes 20 MCP tools over stdio. The game accepts
+bounded typed requests on a private Unix socket and applies edits on its main
+thread. MCP is currently supported on Linux, in single-player editing only.
+
+## Build
+
+The default `make -C src` build and the standalone server/master do not include
+MCP, cJSON or libcrypto. Their existing build dependencies are unchanged.
+The bundled upstream ENet is used in both modes.
+
+To build the bridge, install the ordinary Sauerbraten development dependencies
+(C/C++ compiler, make, SDL2, SDL2_image, SDL2_mixer, zlib and OpenGL), plus
+OpenSSL development headers/libcrypto, then run:
+
+```sh
+make -C src -j2 MCP=1 client server master
+# Equivalent convenience wrapper for the enabled client:
+tools/build-mcp.sh -j2 client
+```
+
+Enabled client objects use `src/.mcp/`, separate from the default objects.
+Switching `MCP=1` on or off does not require `make clean`. Even in an enabled
+build the socket is off until `-mcpbridge<absolute-path>` is supplied.
+The socket option and native validation/test CLI exist only in enabled builds.
+No network listener or MCP SDK is added to the game.
+
+The Python MCP server is maintained separately in
+[sauerbraten-mcp](https://github.com/pastukhov/sauerbraten-mcp). Install it there
+with Python >=3.11 and `uv sync --locked`. No Python SDK is needed to build or
+test this native bridge. cJSON 1.7.19 is vendored under `src/vendor/cjson/` with
+its original MIT license and checked source hashes. Existing Sauerbraten
+notices/licenses remain unchanged.
+
+## Launch and connect
+
+Run from a complete Sauerbraten checkout with its `data/` and `packages/`:
+
+```sh
+umask 077
+sauer_runtime=$(mktemp -d "${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/tmp}/sauer-mcp.XXXXXX")
+printf 'MCP socket: %s/editor.sock\n' "$sauer_runtime"
+tools/run-editor.sh \
+  --client "$PWD/src/sauer_client" \
+  --data-root "$PWD" \
+  --profile "$HOME/.local/share/sauerbraten-mcp" \
+  --socket "$sauer_runtime/editor.sock"
+```
+
+The launcher uses a dedicated profile and redirects game output to that
+profile's `client.log`. Create/open a map in the native UI and enter edit mode.
+In a second terminal or in the MCP host, run the server with the printed path:
+
+```sh
+uv run --project /absolute/sauerbraten-mcp sauer-mcp \
+  --client /absolute/checkout/src/sauer_client \
+  --socket /absolute/private-directory/editor.sock
+```
+
+For an MCP host configure the same `uv` command/arguments as a stdio server.
+Use absolute paths; explicitly passing `--client` also works with a wheel
+installation outside the source tree. The server attaches only: it does not
+start or stop the game. Restarting the server can reconnect to the same game.
+One native peer is allowed; another receives BUSY. The socket is mode 0600,
+its parent must be private mode 0700 and peers must have the same UID.
+
+## Tools and tokens
+
+| Purpose | Tools |
+| --- | --- |
+| Observe | editor_state, region_read, entity_list, texture_catalog, mapmodel_catalog |
+| Geometry | geometry_fill, texture_apply, material_apply |
+| Entities | entity_create, entity_update, entity_delete |
+| History | history_undo, history_redo |
+| View | camera_set, view_capture |
+| Maps and recovery | map_catalog, map_new, map_open, map_save_as, operation_status |
+
+Read `editor_state` before editing and obtain resource refs from the catalogs.
+Each mutation requires a fresh request_id UUID, current map_epoch and
+expected_revision. Revisions/generations are canonical decimal strings, not
+JSON floating-point numbers. Keep the UUID and exact input if a reply is lost;
+ask operation_status before deciding what to do. The bridge does not retry a
+mutation automatically, and unknown does not mean it is safe to repeat it.
+Reusing a UUID for different input is rejected.
+
+Selections specify integer world-coordinate `origin`, `count` in cells,
+power-of-two `grid`, and orient 0..5 (-X,+X,-Y,+Y,-Z,+Z). Bounds use world-unit
+`extent`. Ranges are half-open. Geometry edits are aligned solid/empty fills;
+texture edits affect the exact requested face or all faces. Entities currently
+support light, playerstart and mapmodel. Generation-bound refs expire on
+delete/history/reload; attached entities/history are rejected.
+
+Native manual edits and MCP edits share undo/redo. Each RPC is a separate step;
+read-only queries preserve the native editing boundary, selection and focus.
+Pending native drags/onrelease commands return BUSY. camera_set selects
+first-person and disables zoom. view_capture requires the current view_revision
+and returns PNG MCP ImageContent plus frame tokens. Native edit-mode material
+overlays can still be toggled with the ordinary M binding.
+
+Full closed input schemas are advertised by tools/list and recorded in
+`contracts/v1.json` in the separate Python repository. Unknown fields and invalid, stale or non-finite inputs
+are also rejected independently inside the game, including under -ffast-math.
+There is no arbitrary CubeScript, shell or file-operation tool.
+
+## Save/load behavior and limits
+
+map_new/map_open refuse to replace an unsaved world. map_open pins the source
+payload, preflights it in a separate SDL/GL client and checks state/dependencies
+again before the main-thread commit. Native loading is destructive; a failure
+after reset reports the new state/recovery reference rather than promising a
+complete rollback. Ordinary edits are blocked while recovery_required is set.
+
+map_save_as publishes a new immutable bundle in the dedicated profile:
+`packages/mcp/<slug>-<request_uuid>/{level.ogz,level.cfg,manifest.json}`.
+It does not overwrite source maps or compact the live vslots/history. Export
+reconstructs the original trusted cfg in a private validator and compares
+semantic content/config fingerprints. Bundles depend on this installation's
+assets and cfg; they are not standalone media packages. Changed or shadowed
+dependencies prevent artifact reopening before reset.
+
+The result includes revision_saved and clean_ack. Edits during validation are
+allowed: the snapshot is saved, but a stale acknowledgement leaves the active
+world dirty. A durable private export journal supports outcome lookup/replay
+after transport failures or server restarts. Published outcomes remain readable
+when the game is offline. Simultaneous identical opens share one preflight and
+commit; cancelling a caller does not cancel that shared operation.
+
+The Python supervisor runs validators via Xvfb/xauth, with a bounded timeout and
+kill/reap. No validation subprocess runs in the render loop. Native save/load
+itself is synchronous and can pause frames. Light baking is not part of MCP;
+lighting_dirty is preserved in exports and may require a native recalculation.
+
+Custom shader declarations/variants/alternate/fast/deferred definitions are
+unsupported in preflight. The shader registry survives native map changes, so
+manual custom shader changes latch export_supported=false for that process;
+map_open/map_new/export then require a game restart. editor_state reports the
+reason. Standard lazy shaders remain supported. Name-dependent cfg and runtime
+definitions that cannot be reconstructed can also disable export.
+
+Mutation budgets: 4096 cells, 65536 visited nodes, 8 MiB snapshot and 16 MiB inverse
+preparation. Reads return at most 256 leaves / 4096 nodes per page. Captures are
+at most 1280x720, with a 10-minute TTL and 64 MiB owned cache. Batch, coop editing,
+vertex/terrain/blend editing and lighting baking are outside this first version.
+
+## Verification
+
+```sh
+make -C src test-mcp-transport test-mcp-build-modes
+make -C src MCP=1 test-mcp
+sh tools/tests/run_editor_smoke.sh
+sha256sum -c src/vendor/cjson/SHA256SUMS
+```
+
+The native target requires Python 3, Xvfb/xauth and actual game assets. It runs
+wire checks, eight build-mode checks and 17 cases after real SDL/GL
+initialization; game globals and GL are not replaced by stubs. Tests use private
+profiles and do not edit a normal player profile. To use a different resource
+root, run `python3 src/tests/mcp/run_native_cases.py --client /absolute/client
+--data /absolute/resources` from the checkout.
+
+Run the Python server's end-to-end suite separately:
+
+```sh
+cd /absolute/sauerbraten-mcp
+SAUER_MCP_ENGINE=/absolute/sauerbraten uv run --locked pytest -q
+```
+
+This includes MCP stdio/SDK calls, geometry/history/entities, PNG capture,
+validated save/reopen, recovery and native/Python wire-fixture agreement. The
+server's stdout contains protocol only. See the Python repository for test
+client/data overrides.
+
+Remove only your own temporary profiles/runtime artifacts. Saved bundles and
+the export journal are persistent outcomes needed for recovery.
diff --git a/tools/build-mcp.sh b/tools/build-mcp.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..354061e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/build-mcp.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+set -eu
+root=$(CDPATH= cd -- "$(dirname -- "$0")/.." && pwd)
+if [ "$#" -eq 0 ]; then set -- client; fi
+exec make -C "$root/src" MCP=1 "$@"
diff --git a/tools/run-editor.sh b/tools/run-editor.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..7a7e1fc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/run-editor.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+set -eu
+client= data_root= profile= socket= dry_run=0
+while [ "$#" -gt 0 ]; do
+  case "$1" in
+    --client) client=$2; shift 2 ;;
+    --data-root) data_root=$2; shift 2 ;;
+    --profile) profile=$2; shift 2 ;;
+    --socket) socket=$2; shift 2 ;;
+    --dry-run) dry_run=1; shift ;;
+    *) printf 'Unknown argument: %s\n' "$1" >&2; exit 2 ;;
+  esac
+done
+for value in "$client" "$data_root" "$profile" "$socket"; do
+  case "$value" in /*) ;; *) printf 'All paths must be absolute\n' >&2; exit 2;; esac
+done
+[ -x "$client" ] && [ -d "$data_root" ] || exit 2
+if [ "$dry_run" = 1 ]; then
+  printf '%s\n' "$client" "-q$profile" "-k$data_root" "-mcpbridge$socket" '-t0'
+  exit
+fi
+umask 077
+mkdir -p "$profile"
+cd "$data_root"
+exec "$client" "-q$profile" "-k$data_root" "-mcpbridge$socket" -t0 > "$profile/client.log" 2>&1
diff --git a/tools/tests/run_editor_smoke.sh b/tools/tests/run_editor_smoke.sh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8ada9e8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/tests/run_editor_smoke.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+set -eu
+repo=$(CDPATH= cd -- "$(dirname -- "$0")/../.." && pwd)
+testroot=$(mktemp -d)
+trap 'rm -rf "$testroot"' EXIT
+mkdir -p "$testroot/data space" "$testroot/profile space"
+printf '#!/bin/sh\nprintf "client output\\n"\nprintf "%%s\\n" "$@" > "$ARG_LOG"\n' > "$testroot/fake client"
+chmod +x "$testroot/fake client"
+ARG_LOG="$testroot/args" "$repo/tools/run-editor.sh" --client "$testroot/fake client" --data-root "$testroot/data space" --profile "$testroot/profile space" --socket "$testroot/bridge.sock" > "$testroot/stdout"
+test ! -s "$testroot/stdout"
+rg -F -- "-q$testroot/profile space" "$testroot/args"
+rg -F -- "-k$testroot/data space" "$testroot/args"
+rg -F -- "-mcpbridge$testroot/bridge.sock" "$testroot/args"
+rg -F 'client output' "$testroot/profile space/client.log"
+printf 'launcher smoke: PASS\n'
